insert_after('At completion, the application exports `mobile-acceptance-evidence.json` containing the target ID, challenge, build identity, origin, test-project identity, operation receipts, console/runtime findings available to the application, screenshots or recording references, exported project digest, performer identity assurance, physical-device assertion, and evidence basis. CI verifies every mechanically verifiable binding before accepting the record. The physical-device fact remains HUMAN_OBSERVATION or stronger external attestation according to the actual evidence and is never mislabeled application-proven.\n','\nThe evidence file reaches CI through the repository as a committed file or authenticated workflow input from a submitter recorded in the acceptance artifact. Each MOBILE_ACCEPTANCE_CHALLENGE is single-use: CI accepts at most one evidence file per challenge and rejects reused, unknown, or expired challenges and any evidence bound to a different commit, manifest, origin, target, or test project; a superseding run requires a new challenge. The gate minimum for the physical-device fact is HUMAN_OBSERVATION by the recorded performer at the recorded identity assurance; that basis is explicitly sufficient and is never relabeled application-proven.\n')
